WEBVTT

00:04.210 --> 00:05.400
We have no money.

00:05.660 --> 00:09.230
Boss, you've said that a 
number of times already.

00:09.500 --> 00:12.320
That's what we're here to discuss, right?

00:12.870 --> 00:16.530
<i>Recovery after the bandit 
raid has proved challenging.</i>

00:17.270 --> 00:23.230
<i>The burden of reopening the two sealed 
villages has proved a heavy one.</i>

00:24.470 --> 00:26.210
<i>Between digging up the filled-in wells,</i>

00:26.650 --> 00:28.490
<i>rebuilding the torn-down homesteads,</i>

00:28.490 --> 00:34.930
<i>and securing food to get through the 
upcoming winter after having to strip the fields,</i>

00:35.880 --> 00:38.300
<i>we're quickly running through our treasury.</i>

00:39.820 --> 00:44.390
Letting that bandit leader 
escape hasn't helped matters.

00:44.610 --> 00:49.980
We'd have secured at least 
200 gold coins for his head.

00:49.980 --> 00:52.380
We can't borrow the money?

00:52.380 --> 00:54.320
Who would lend it out to us?

00:54.320 --> 00:58.200
Every nearby fief has nothing 
to spare, thanks to the frost.

00:58.470 --> 01:02.780
Some have even been asking <i>us</i> for loans!

01:02.780 --> 01:04.630
What about the court nobles?

01:05.290 --> 01:06.650
Not a chance!

01:06.650 --> 01:12.420
That band of misers would charge 
a gold piece of interest!

01:12.850 --> 01:13.760
Say...

01:14.890 --> 01:19.550
Can't you and Mother ask 
your parents for help?

01:19.550 --> 01:23.970
I'm afraid Agnes and I both 
cut ties with our parents.

01:23.970 --> 01:25.520
A long time ago.

01:26.210 --> 01:28.490
I've never even introduced 
them to their grandchildren.

01:28.490 --> 01:32.030
I can't exactly ask them about money now.

01:32.030 --> 01:33.610
I see.

01:34.220 --> 01:36.860
When your mother and I first met,

01:37.360 --> 01:39.930
my lands were even more 
barren than they are now.

01:39.930 --> 01:43.080
Everyone around us opposed the union.

01:43.400 --> 01:48.040
And after a whirlwind love affair,
 they basically eloped!

01:48.320 --> 01:50.170
Gotta say, I'm pretty jealous!

01:51.000 --> 01:53.690
<i>When the norm in this world 
is arranged marriages...</i>

01:53.690 --> 01:55.450
<i>It must have been really hard on them.</i>

01:55.450 --> 01:57.850
Anyway, we have no money!

01:57.850 --> 02:00.230
Yeah, we know that already!

02:04.220 --> 02:09.270
<i>This is the tale of a genius patissier 
who died before his time,</i>

02:09.480 --> 02:13.490
<i>and was reincarnated as the son 
of a poor noble in another world</i>

02:13.490 --> 02:16.650
<i>to pursue a world full 
of desserts and smiles.</i>

02:17.530 --> 02:22.240
<i>It's a tale that is at once cold 
and unsparing, and syrupy sweet.</i>

02:23.690 --> 02:30.090
<i>His dream is to create this 
world's very own land of sweets!</i>

02:38.050 --> 02:40.630
<b>Sweet Reincarnation</b>

04:02.610 --> 04:08.660
<b>A Spicy Negotiation and Sweet Baked Treats</b>

04:03.520 --> 04:10.020
So that's what you guys have been 
discussing in your dad's office for days?

04:10.020 --> 04:10.640
Yeah.

04:10.640 --> 04:14.480
Pas... don't hide stuff from us.
 It's really untouchable.

04:14.720 --> 04:16.550
Dummy. You mean "unsociable."

04:16.550 --> 04:18.190
I know that!

04:18.520 --> 04:20.700
Lumi, how are you healing up?

04:20.700 --> 04:22.650
Do you have permission 
to be out here right now?

04:23.140 --> 04:26.780
Yeah, Dad and Grandpa both said 
it's okay if I'm out and about.

04:26.780 --> 04:28.090
See?

04:28.650 --> 04:29.740
Ow!

04:30.560 --> 04:32.620
The pain's not totally gone, though.

04:33.120 --> 04:35.250
Sheesh. Take it easy, would you?

04:35.250 --> 04:37.040
C'mon, I'm fine!

04:38.030 --> 04:38.840
What's so funny?

04:39.400 --> 04:41.520
You just make such a cute couple!

04:41.520 --> 04:44.930
I <i>told</i> you, it ain't like that!

04:46.000 --> 04:48.670
So, what about making the fields bigger?

04:49.140 --> 04:52.640
There's still room in our 
lands to expand, it's true.

04:52.970 --> 04:57.130
But to do so requires time, 
manpower, and most of all, money.

04:57.450 --> 04:59.680
It might not be happening any time soon.

04:59.680 --> 05:02.650
What about that bonka pie you made before?

05:02.650 --> 05:03.740
Bonka pie?

05:04.690 --> 05:06.240
That was super tasty!

05:06.240 --> 05:08.090
Why not sell them in town?

05:09.830 --> 05:12.040
They're fun to make, it's true...

05:14.700 --> 05:19.650
<i>Yes... so very much fun...</i>

05:23.130 --> 05:25.870
<i>No, no! We're here to 
make </i>money<i>, not desserts!</i>

05:25.870 --> 05:28.010
In order to produce enough 
to make a profit,

05:28.010 --> 05:30.880
we'd need a way to bring in a lot of bonkas.

05:30.880 --> 05:32.720
It probably wouldn't work.

05:32.720 --> 05:36.810
Why not teach magic, then?

05:36.810 --> 05:39.730
Why do you want to learn magic?

05:39.730 --> 05:42.890
You can do big things with magic, right?

05:43.210 --> 05:47.150
I'd make myself rich and 
eat tasty things every day!

05:47.530 --> 05:48.810
What a joke.

05:49.210 --> 05:51.190
It'd take a miracle for you to learn magic.

05:51.190 --> 05:55.120
And even if you did learn how to use it,

05:55.120 --> 05:58.500
there's no way <i>you'd</i> use 
it effectively, Marc.

05:58.500 --> 05:59.960
What's that supposed to mean?!

06:00.220 --> 06:01.850
I'm saying, if you learned a fire spell,

06:01.850 --> 06:05.120
the best you'd do is set fire to yourself!

06:05.480 --> 06:07.800
Because you're <i>stupid</i>!

06:07.800 --> 06:09.930
D-Don't make fun of me!

06:10.170 --> 06:12.720
Okay, okay. Enough flirting.

06:12.720 --> 06:14.260
It ain't flirting, damn it!

06:14.640 --> 06:17.410
Still, magic could still be the key!

06:17.410 --> 06:19.110
Magic?

06:19.440 --> 06:22.680
Why not show us that spell you use, Pas?

06:22.680 --> 06:24.090
Something might come up!

06:24.090 --> 06:25.570
Hey, great idea!

06:27.610 --> 06:29.900
<i>"Three heads is better," as they say...</i>

06:29.900 --> 06:32.120
<i>They really might point 
me in the right direction!</i>

06:33.390 --> 06:36.730
<i>When I was thinking up new 
sweets back in my old world,</i>

06:37.400 --> 06:41.330
<i>I'd spend all night brainstorming 
with my colleagues!</i>

06:42.380 --> 06:43.450
All right.

06:43.830 --> 06:47.090
Draw any picture you like in the dirt.

06:47.380 --> 06:49.060
Can we draw anything?

06:49.060 --> 06:49.860
Yes.

06:55.090 --> 06:56.580
What's this one?

06:58.210 --> 07:01.850
It's me, totally wasting a dragon with magic!

07:02.230 --> 07:04.570
Oh... is that supposed to be a dragon?

07:04.860 --> 07:06.060
Really?

07:06.060 --> 07:08.500
<i>I thought it was a worm with legs.</i>

07:10.790 --> 07:13.680
Lumi, is that a bonka, then?

07:13.680 --> 07:14.490
Yep!

07:15.740 --> 07:17.270
Pretty good, right?

07:17.270 --> 07:18.350
And next to it?

07:18.350 --> 07:20.210
A bonka pie, of course!

07:21.290 --> 07:23.670
I thought it was a rock. You suck at drawing.

07:24.050 --> 07:25.160
What was that?

07:25.160 --> 07:28.380
Yours just looks like a slithering snake!

07:28.380 --> 07:32.420
Can't you see how cool my dragon is?!

07:32.420 --> 07:34.270
Only a little kid would think that!

07:34.270 --> 07:35.250
Okay, okay!

07:35.250 --> 07:37.600
I'm gonna use my spell now!

07:40.820 --> 07:41.770
Replicate!

08:02.680 --> 08:04.230
Awesome!

08:04.230 --> 08:05.710
It put the picture on me!

08:06.170 --> 08:09.850
Wow! Pas, you really can use magic!

08:09.850 --> 08:12.050
Well, you've seen me use it before...

08:14.430 --> 08:16.310
It's not rubbing off.

08:16.310 --> 08:19.010
On skin, it disappears 
after about three days.

08:19.630 --> 08:22.270
It's permanent on trees or walls, though.

08:22.650 --> 08:24.230
That's so awesome!

08:25.410 --> 08:27.370
I wanna show it to Grandpa!

08:27.770 --> 08:30.440
Hey, Pas. Can you do it the other way?

08:31.670 --> 08:33.290
The other way... how?

08:34.440 --> 08:36.620
Instead of copying a drawing onto something,

08:37.130 --> 08:39.390
could you copy something else as a drawing?

08:39.790 --> 08:42.080
Copy something... as a drawing?

08:42.380 --> 08:45.510
If you could put a picture of a house 
or someone's face on the ground,

08:46.040 --> 08:48.260
I think that'd be pretty cool!

08:48.260 --> 08:50.550
That don't make no sense!

08:50.930 --> 08:51.600
Dork.

08:51.600 --> 08:52.610
What was that?!

08:52.610 --> 08:54.260
Mega-dork!

08:54.260 --> 08:55.740
That's it!

08:56.800 --> 08:58.060
That's it!

08:58.060 --> 08:59.140
Yes, that's it!

08:59.140 --> 09:00.760
Lumi, you're a genius!

09:03.730 --> 09:05.850
Hey, where'd that come from?!

09:05.850 --> 09:08.730
Sorry to put my hands on your wife, Marc.

09:08.730 --> 09:11.070
Put that gag to rest, would ya?

09:11.440 --> 09:14.520
But you gave me such a great idea!

09:16.390 --> 09:17.490
I see.

09:17.710 --> 09:20.860
Are our finances that tight?

09:22.200 --> 09:27.290
But... I'm not sure my 
parents will offer much aid.

09:28.630 --> 09:30.770
I see. I'm sorry to ask...

09:31.390 --> 09:32.380
Father!

09:33.500 --> 09:35.720
I've got a great way to make money!

09:36.000 --> 09:37.460
You mean it, kid?

09:37.460 --> 09:38.930
What is it?

09:39.210 --> 09:43.250
You told me about your attempts to 
arrange a marriage for Josie, right?

09:43.680 --> 09:44.890
Y-Yes...

09:45.290 --> 09:47.370
The little lady's thirteen years old now.

09:47.370 --> 09:49.980
She's just about marrying age!

09:50.370 --> 09:52.980
Since you have your teleportation spell,

09:52.980 --> 09:58.070
you could take her all around 
to introduce her, right?

09:58.360 --> 10:03.410
Yes, and I was happy for the chance to 
show off my wonderful daughter, as well...

10:03.790 --> 10:07.770
What do parents who don't have 
that sort of magic available do?

10:08.420 --> 10:14.880
The most efficient way is to attend 
a royal ball at the capital.

10:14.880 --> 10:18.220
Yes, and travel can prove so dangerous...

10:18.540 --> 10:21.130
Indeed, and it's far from free!

10:21.130 --> 10:25.680
They say that when a noble travels, 
their money sprouts wings and flies away!

10:25.680 --> 10:29.530
What if we sold something like this, then?

10:30.420 --> 10:31.650
Replicate!

10:36.130 --> 10:37.220
Goodness!

10:38.480 --> 10:39.460
Look at that!

10:40.160 --> 10:42.030
It looks just like her!

10:42.340 --> 10:44.740
It's like looking in a mirror!

10:45.250 --> 10:47.830
I call them "matchmaking photos."

10:48.490 --> 10:50.520
"Ask the heir to the Fief 
of Morteln to use his magic

10:50.520 --> 10:52.120
to make you a matchmaking photo,

10:52.570 --> 10:57.080
and you can show off your child 
without the need for travel."

10:57.080 --> 11:02.500
That can be our pitch to parents 
seeking arranged marriages!

11:03.680 --> 11:07.600
<i>I guess knowledge unrelated 
to sweets can come in handy too!</i>

11:09.490 --> 11:13.560
<i>We could fetch five or ten gold 
coins for a picture this detailed...</i>

11:14.260 --> 11:16.560
<i>It's still cheaper than a proper portrait,</i>

11:16.560 --> 11:19.400
<i>and because it's magic, we don't 
have to charge for materials.</i>

11:20.090 --> 11:25.060
<i>Plenty of parents would pay out the nose 
to introduce their child with a picture.</i>

11:26.810 --> 11:28.450
This might just work.

11:28.450 --> 11:32.040
But the nature of the kid's 
magic will get out like this.

11:32.040 --> 11:33.340
Do we want to risk it?

11:33.340 --> 11:36.320
It's not as if we'd be 
able to hide it forever.

11:36.800 --> 11:41.610
And letting people think my magic 
is just about making pictures

11:41.610 --> 11:45.160
might let me hide in plain sight.

11:46.570 --> 11:48.050
I see.

11:48.050 --> 11:49.140
All right.

11:49.140 --> 11:52.750
Let's start by feeling 
out Count Retes about it.

11:50.810 --> 11:52.000
Pas, my love?

11:52.000 --> 11:52.750
Yes?

11:52.750 --> 11:54.330
Look at this part here.

11:55.540 --> 11:56.980
These crow's feet...

11:56.980 --> 11:58.410
Can you erase them?

12:02.920 --> 12:05.270
<i>Located in the south of the 
Divine Kingdom of Praulich,</i>

12:05.270 --> 12:06.840
<i>the County of Retes is an outlying domain</i>

12:06.840 --> 12:09.610
<i>bordered to the east and south by the sea.</i>

12:09.970 --> 12:14.980
<i>Over fifty villages lie within 
its borders, with four main villages.</i>

12:16.410 --> 12:21.750
<i>They're all linked by roads to the 
local capital, which administrates them.</i>

12:22.190 --> 12:24.270
<i>It's one of the largest domains in the south.</i>

12:24.930 --> 12:28.810
<i>At the core of it all is the 
local capital, Retesvale.</i>

12:24.990 --> 12:29.260
<b>County of Retes   Retesvale</b>

12:29.550 --> 12:32.730
I have come seeking a 
meeting with Count Retes.

12:32.960 --> 12:35.200
I ask for safe passage within.

12:35.200 --> 12:36.940
We've been expecting you.

12:37.560 --> 12:42.150
Has he come to take me to task for 
failing to crush the bandit threat?

12:42.410 --> 12:47.490
Chastisement from a mere backwater 
noble is nothing to fear.

12:48.720 --> 12:49.810
Perhaps so.

12:50.490 --> 12:53.550
I'll butter him up and send him on his way.

12:57.460 --> 13:00.720
Mistress, the Lord of Morteln has arrived.

13:01.340 --> 13:02.920
Allow him in.

13:03.830 --> 13:06.200
We are pleased to have you here, milord.

13:06.200 --> 13:10.140
I could not be more honored to 
meet the famous Lord of Morteln.

13:10.610 --> 13:12.940
I am the holder of the 
borderland fief of Retes,

13:10.870 --> 13:16.230
<b>Brioche Salgrade Mille Retes</b>

13:13.250 --> 13:16.230
Brioche Salgrade Mille Retes.

13:18.250 --> 13:19.690
Listen to me, Pas.

13:20.000 --> 13:23.050
She's the eldest daughter 
of the previous Count Retes.

13:23.760 --> 13:25.940
Her predecessors died in conflict,

13:25.940 --> 13:31.240
and her only rightful heir 
was very young at the time.

13:31.680 --> 13:37.040
Brioche was allowed to assume authority 
until that heir came of age.

13:37.040 --> 13:39.080
So she's the current holder of the fief?

13:40.650 --> 13:45.220
But the heir died before he came of age.

13:45.630 --> 13:50.180
I am so grateful to have this 
time with you, Count Retes.

13:50.930 --> 13:54.120
My, what a charming young gentleman.

13:56.330 --> 13:57.820
<i>She seems genial enough...</i>

13:58.200 --> 14:01.270
<i>But she's watching us very closely.</i>

14:05.770 --> 14:08.180
Would you join me for tea?

14:08.180 --> 14:09.870
I would be delighted.

14:14.910 --> 14:16.200
<i>Look at those!</i>

14:16.200 --> 14:18.290
<i>Baked treats... cookies!</i>

14:18.290 --> 14:21.180
Tea is one of our household businesses.

14:21.180 --> 14:24.000
We've prepared only the 
finest for your visit.

14:24.000 --> 14:28.570
The teas of Retes are well known 
even in the royal capital.

14:31.610 --> 14:33.310
Yes, truly excellent.

14:33.810 --> 14:37.170
The aroma and flavor both 
live up to their reputation.

14:37.170 --> 14:39.610
I'm truly pleased to hear that.

14:42.430 --> 14:45.180
<i>I used to make cookies all the time!</i>

14:45.510 --> 14:48.570
<i>The time and temperature until 
you bake them is most important!</i>

14:52.490 --> 14:54.330
<i>It's kind of...</i>

14:55.530 --> 15:00.500
<i>Most children are thrilled to 
receive sweet things of any kind.</i>

15:00.810 --> 15:02.020
<b>Slurp...</b>

15:02.060 --> 15:03.210
<b>Hmmmmm</b>

15:03.720 --> 15:06.510
I see you excel at more 
than just military matters.

15:06.510 --> 15:09.620
To extract such bounties from a barren land

15:09.620 --> 15:12.560
suggests you're a wonderful leader as well.

15:12.560 --> 15:14.180
You flatter me.

15:14.180 --> 15:19.640
I'd love to learn your secrets 
of agricultural administration.

15:19.640 --> 15:22.550
Surely you overestimate me, my lady.

15:22.550 --> 15:26.780
A large part of why the land can 
support its people so well now

15:26.780 --> 15:29.450
is because of my son's advice.

15:29.450 --> 15:31.740
I myself have done very little.

15:31.970 --> 15:33.980
My, such humility!

15:33.980 --> 15:36.760
While I shamefully struggle 
just to keep my lands together,

15:36.760 --> 15:40.180
you refuse to take pride in 
your many accomplishments.

15:41.190 --> 15:47.770
<i>I suppose it does seem unbelievable 
for a child not yet ten years old</i>

15:47.770 --> 15:49.710
<i>to oversee the cultivation of a wasteland.</i>

15:52.300 --> 15:57.180
You must be proud to have 
such a fine man for a father.

15:57.420 --> 15:59.790
<i>She's finally talking to me.</i>

15:59.790 --> 16:00.740
<i>Now's my chance!</i>

16:00.740 --> 16:04.660
Yes, we owe our household's 
prosperity to my father!

16:04.970 --> 16:06.730
I'm sure you do!

16:08.090 --> 16:11.370
But the fief into which my father 
poured his sweat and tears

16:11.370 --> 16:13.450
recently came under terrible attack.

16:14.320 --> 16:16.620
A raid by several hundred bandits.

16:16.620 --> 16:20.010
Even I and my fellow children 
were forced to take up arms.

16:20.570 --> 16:21.660
Several hundred?

16:22.210 --> 16:24.350
<i>It was actually just about fifty,</i>

16:24.730 --> 16:26.050
<i>but it's to my advantage to lie.</i>

16:26.050 --> 16:29.590
<i>Exaggeration to throw her 
off is a negotiating tactic.</i>

16:27.350 --> 16:28.910
Oh, is that so?

16:29.830 --> 16:31.010
<i>Damnation!</i>

16:31.010 --> 16:33.080
<i>I let the child broach the subject.</i>

16:34.140 --> 16:38.300
It's splendid to see you assuming the 
duties of nobility at such a young age.

16:38.300 --> 16:40.890
Our household could truly 
learn from your example!

16:41.140 --> 16:44.350
And when we interrogated 
the bandits we'd captured,

16:44.780 --> 16:47.670
they admitted they'd come out of Retesvale.

16:49.340 --> 16:51.710
<i>He's going to negotiate for damages.</i>

16:51.710 --> 16:53.150
<i>I should plead ignorance.</i>

16:53.720 --> 16:55.380
Gracious, could such a thing be true?

16:55.380 --> 16:56.700
I'd heard nothing of it.

16:56.920 --> 17:01.110
If you doubt my words, we're prepared 
to turn a few bandits over to you.

17:02.550 --> 17:04.570
If that fails to spark your memory,

17:04.570 --> 17:06.560
we could hand them directly 
over to the royal family.

17:06.560 --> 17:09.340
That could lead to an 
official investigation...

17:09.630 --> 17:11.000
But would you prefer that?

17:11.350 --> 17:12.420
<i>This child...</i>

17:12.850 --> 17:15.630
Then, assuming your theory is correct,

17:15.920 --> 17:19.850
perhaps it's a band that our household 
eradicated within our territory,

17:19.850 --> 17:22.680
and the few remaining stragglers 
escaped into yours.

17:24.110 --> 17:28.260
It seems that attempts to stamp out bandits 
in the County of Retes have failed.

17:29.770 --> 17:36.400
The bandits claimed they moved on after 
<i>shaking off</i> pursuit in your domain.

17:36.730 --> 17:39.140
If you claim that your household 
eradicated the bandits,

17:39.140 --> 17:42.660
whose forces did they shake off?

17:42.660 --> 17:44.500
Who did they fight?

17:45.880 --> 17:48.210
Well, I fear I couldn't say.

17:48.730 --> 17:51.240
Do you have any proof that 
the bandits we eradicated

17:51.240 --> 17:53.030
and the ones you captured

17:53.030 --> 17:55.780
are the same set of bandits?

18:00.050 --> 18:02.680
One of the bandits was carrying it.

18:02.680 --> 18:04.930
It carries your family crest.

18:06.730 --> 18:08.650
That's... one of my men's...

18:08.650 --> 18:10.010
<i>They've got me.</i>

18:10.920 --> 18:14.830
From our perspective, it seems your 
eradication of the bandits failed,

18:15.560 --> 18:20.540
and they raided our fief as 
a result of your failure.

18:21.330 --> 18:23.410
It would be difficult to say.

18:23.410 --> 18:25.540
We understand your position, of course.

18:25.920 --> 18:29.400
We have no intention of causing 
trouble over this incident.

18:29.400 --> 18:31.130
I would be terribly grateful for that.

18:31.130 --> 18:33.500
However, even if they were mere stragglers,

18:33.500 --> 18:35.550
the bandits still came out of your territory.

18:36.020 --> 18:41.090
Compensation for our trouble 
would be greatly appreciated.

18:41.090 --> 18:42.720
Compensation, you say?

18:44.090 --> 18:48.060
I'm sure we can find an appropriate amount.

18:48.060 --> 18:51.040
A hundred gold coins, perhaps?

18:51.620 --> 18:56.150
And damages. Surely we deserve 
to be made whole again as well?

18:56.410 --> 18:58.740
You don't speak like a child, do you?

18:59.310 --> 19:01.740
A hundred and thirty, then.

19:01.740 --> 19:03.200
Try again.

19:13.930 --> 19:15.450
A hundred and fifty.

19:16.700 --> 19:18.210
Acceptable, perhaps.

19:18.470 --> 19:20.580
What do you think, Father?

19:20.580 --> 19:21.300
Agreed.

19:23.690 --> 19:24.880
<i>This child...</i>

19:25.690 --> 19:27.240
<i>He's exceptional.</i>

19:30.280 --> 19:33.000
<i>Perhaps the Lord of Morteln's words before</i>

19:33.370 --> 19:35.830
<i>were more than mere humility.</i>

19:36.420 --> 19:39.560
<i>Normally, it is the father who 
would conduct negotiations.</i>

19:40.180 --> 19:41.370
<i>And yet...</i>

19:42.650 --> 19:44.600
<i>Still, 150 gold coins,</i>

19:44.600 --> 19:47.910
<i>against the possibility 
of losing the king's trust</i>

19:47.910 --> 19:50.850
<i>for letting bandits escape 
and ravage nearby lands...</i>

19:50.850 --> 19:52.380
<i>It's a small price to pay.</i>

19:54.490 --> 19:57.300
Father, it's 150 even!

20:02.550 --> 20:06.710
Perhaps I underestimated you due to your age.

20:06.710 --> 20:08.800
I must admit defeat.

20:09.150 --> 20:12.440
A hope you'll forgive me for 
the impertinent things I said.

20:12.810 --> 20:15.900
I don't believe you've introduced yourself.

20:16.570 --> 20:18.010
An unfortunate lapse. Forgive me.

20:18.630 --> 20:22.910
I am the son of Casserole 
Mille Morteln, Pastry.

20:23.340 --> 20:25.870
It's been a pleasure to 
make your acquaintance.

20:26.240 --> 20:27.610
Pastry...

20:27.610 --> 20:29.420
<i>I'll remember that.</i>

20:29.420 --> 20:32.120
Might I ask you one thing?

20:32.120 --> 20:32.710
Yes?

20:33.210 --> 20:37.670
You seemed rather displeased 
by the tea we served earlier.

20:39.120 --> 20:40.270
Oh...

20:40.270 --> 20:41.370
Was there a problem with it?

20:41.370 --> 20:44.380
Oh, no... the tea was excellent.

20:44.620 --> 20:45.690
But...

20:45.690 --> 20:46.560
But?

20:46.560 --> 20:50.850
I thought the accompaniments 
were perhaps overly sweet.

20:51.560 --> 20:52.310
Oh?

20:52.690 --> 20:54.910
When serving baked treats with tea,

20:54.910 --> 20:59.730
a more modest sweetness 
might prove more appealing!

20:59.960 --> 21:03.510
Why not make something less sweet next time?

21:00.410 --> 21:01.370
Pas!

21:03.510 --> 21:06.600
It would allow the aroma of 
the tea to assert itself,

21:06.600 --> 21:09.700
and make both the tea and 
sweets far more enjoyable!

21:10.050 --> 21:13.910
Gracious... what a refined palate you have.

21:13.910 --> 21:15.250
To reduce the sweetness—

21:15.350 --> 21:18.210
<b>Bonk</b>

21:15.350 --> 21:18.210
<b>Bonk</b>

21:15.350 --> 21:18.210
<b>Bonk</b>

21:15.350 --> 21:18.210
<b>Bonk</b>

21:15.350 --> 21:18.210
<b>Bonk</b>

21:15.350 --> 21:18.210
<b>Bonk</b>

21:15.350 --> 21:18.210
<b>Bonk</b>

21:15.350 --> 21:18.210
<b>Bonk</b>

21:15.350 --> 21:18.210
<b>Bonk</b>

21:15.350 --> 21:18.210
<b>Bonk</b>

21:16.170 --> 21:18.210
Pas!

21:20.180 --> 21:21.800
A thousand apologies.

21:23.210 --> 21:27.390
<i>I thought he was 
merely precocious, but perhaps...</i>

21:23.970 --> 21:26.490
We should take our leave now.

21:26.490 --> 21:27.390
Right...

21:27.930 --> 21:31.690
Forgive me for arriving with no gift in hand.

21:31.690 --> 21:33.710
Perhaps you'll take this instead.

21:35.580 --> 21:36.410
<i>Replicate.</i>

21:53.160 --> 21:54.620
It's most delightful.

21:55.070 --> 21:56.090
Thank you.

21:57.170 --> 22:00.190
A show of gratitude for the delicious tea,

22:00.190 --> 22:02.990
and Your Ladyship's most 
gracious consideration.

23:36.940 --> 23:39.000
Next time on <i>Sweet Reincarnation</i>...

23:39.000 --> 23:42.220
"Sweet Matchmaking Photos and Twin Ladies."

23:39.080 --> 23:44.980
<b>Sweet Matchmaking Photos and Twin Ladies</b>

23:42.220 --> 23:43.580
Bon appétit!

23:44.980 --> 23:50.250
<b>Illustration:</b>

23:44.980 --> 23:50.250
<b>Bantya Shibano</b>
